## Project status, funding & disclaimer

- **Open-source & unfunded.** This is an unfunded, volunteer, open-source assistive-technology project (MIT / R.O.A.R. / TSSFAA). It is provided **as-is**, for community reuse and reproduction.
- **Sources.** Some information here draws on manufacturer datasheets, standards, and **non-peer-reviewed sources** (vendor documentation, maker-community reports) alongside peer-reviewed literature. Claims should be independently verified before being relied on; reference entries are flagged where bibliographic details or peer-review status are unconfirmed.
- **No medical or FDA claims.** The authors make **no assertion** that this device, the Air Isolator, or any component is FDA-cleared, FDA-registered, biocompatibility-certified, or compliant with any medical-device regulation in any jurisdiction. Nothing here is a medical claim, a safety certification, or a substitute for professional or regulatory evaluation. The hygiene and material guidance is **design intent, not a validated infection-control or biocompatibility protocol.**
- **Use at your own risk.** Anyone fabricating or deploying this — especially for vulnerable users or clinical/shared settings — is responsible for their own safety validation, biocompatibility testing, and regulatory compliance in their jurisdiction.

